[LESSON]: Alloy 6 does not allow 'run' or 'check' commands for predicates/assertions that are structurally unsatisfiable due to overconstraints; scenario predicates must not overconstrain transitions, but should existentially witness allowed behavior.
[LESSON]: In predicates modeling behavior over states, to show a property is possible, require only the minimal transition and not more than one processed/pending status unless the fact requires it; overconstraining (for example, requiring all other requests remain pending) can make the predicate unsat.
[LESSON]: When debugging existential assertions, running the corresponding predicate directly (with 'run') is effective for isolating whether the model/facts permit the scenario at all.
[LESSON]: Facts that are conditional on mode (e.g., mutex only enforced in Normal) must be carefully checked so they do not inadvertently constrain Emergency behavior through other logic.
