**[LESSON]: Can't use 'in' operator with set comprehensions in Alloy 6 → Must use explicit set comprehensions like {u: User | ...}**  
**[LESSON]: Alloy 6 requires explicit type annotations for all predicate parameters and uses commas to separate them**  
**[LESSON]: Alloy 6 does not support parameterized open of util/seq → Must use 'open util/seq as Seq' and refer to Seq[Type]**  
**[LESSON]: Alloy 6 does not allow inline comments at the end of 'open' statements → Comments must be on a separate line**  
**[LESSON]: After 'open util/seq[Request]', Seq[Request] type is in scope directly, no 'util/seq/' or alias prefix needed**
